00:01:08.020 --> 00:01:11.969
Now in order to discuss the full plan we have
to talk about how hard up that Marvel were

00:01:11.969 --> 00:01:16.170
in the 90s as it massively effects the way
that the plan was laid out.

00:01:16.170 --> 00:01:22.170
Marvel Studios started up in the 90s and it
mainly worked as a part of it's parent company

00:01:22.170 --> 00:01:23.289
that dealt with licences.

00:01:23.289 --> 00:01:27.749
This involved the office selling off major
characters to other studios so that the company

00:01:27.749 --> 00:01:28.749
could keep afloat.

00:01:28.749 --> 00:01:32.069
I'm sure you've heard the story about how
they had to sell office equipment to other

00:01:32.069 --> 00:01:36.509
places just to keep the lights on and they
had truly fallen from greatness.

00:01:36.509 --> 00:01:41.340
In this time they lost the film rights to
Spider-man, The X-men, Fantastic Four, Hulk

00:01:41.340 --> 00:01:43.310
and all their flagship characters.

00:01:43.310 --> 00:01:46.920
Hulk did sort of get a co-operative deal with
Universal but it was pretty much the company

00:01:46.920 --> 00:01:51.009
trying to scramble for as much cash as they
could before it all came crashing down.

00:01:51.009 --> 00:01:55.979
In 1996 they filed for bankruptcie but slowly
they managed to claw their way back.

00:01:55.979 --> 00:02:00.850
At the time, American Businessman Carl Icahn
started buying bonds in the company at 20%

00:02:00.850 --> 00:02:03.759
of their value and he eventually took over
the company.

00:02:03.759 --> 00:02:09.060
In 1997 during the bankruptcy renegotiation
phase Toy Biz then bought Marvel from the

00:02:09.060 --> 00:02:14.069
banks and shortly after this it was taken
over once more by Ron Perelman who regained

00:02:14.069 --> 00:02:15.709
control once more.

00:02:15.709 --> 00:02:19.540
Slowly it was pulled out of bankruptcy and
it would go onto become the juggernaut that

00:02:19.540 --> 00:02:21.240
we now know it as today.

00:02:21.240 --> 00:02:25.790
Now in 1998 the company got somewhat of a
big revival in the mainstream with the release

00:02:25.790 --> 00:02:26.879
of Blade

00:02:26.879 --> 00:02:31.739
Blade was a big gamble for them and under
the name Marvel Enterprises the film released

00:02:31.739 --> 00:02:38.180
to positive reviews and also a box office
of 131 million off the back of a 45 million

00:02:38.180 --> 00:02:39.180
budget.

00:02:39.180 --> 00:02:47.150
It wouldn't be long before other studios started
to propel the property purchases that they'd

00:02:47.150 --> 00:02:50.719
bought and we saw the X-men and Spider-man
drop to great success.

00:02:50.719 --> 00:02:55.549
This also got a lot of interest in the comics
and Marvel sales slowly but surely started

00:02:55.549 --> 00:02:56.549
to pick up.

00:02:56.549 --> 00:03:00.379
They got a lot of secondary gains from selling
this stuff and the brand related income that

00:03:00.379 --> 00:03:03.930
came in from merchandising offered them new
opportunities.

00:03:03.930 --> 00:03:08.980
Marvel Studios started to look at self financing
in 2004 and they put together in place a plan

00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:10.520
to make ten films.

00:03:10.520 --> 00:03:14.629
This was going to span across an 8 year window
with us getting roughly one a year but in

00:03:14.629 --> 00:03:16.460
some instances two.

00:03:16.460 --> 00:03:19.909
It's important to bear in mind that they didn't
own the rights to Iron Man at this time and

00:03:19.909 --> 00:03:22.760
thus he's not included in the original plan.

00:03:22.760 --> 00:03:27.830
New Line owned him up to November 2005 and
then when they were released it vastly altered

00:03:27.830 --> 00:03:29.670
what they were going to do.

00:03:29.670 --> 00:03:32.249
What they wanted to create though was this.

00:03:32.249 --> 00:03:37.090
A Captain America movie that started it all
off, an Avengers one, Nick Fury, Hawkeye,

00:03:37.090 --> 00:03:41.749
Power Pack, Shang-Chi Black Panther, Ant-Man
and Cloak And Dagger.

00:03:41.749 --> 00:03:47.000
Now the one that probably stands out to you
the most there is The Avengers who would've

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:48.939
had a completely different line-up.

00:03:48.939 --> 00:03:52.569
We don't know the specifics here but Nick
Fury would've followed the same role that

00:03:52.569 --> 00:03:54.719
he did in the eventual Phase 1 that we got.

00:03:54.719 --> 00:03:59.750
He'd go round recruiting the other members
of the team and they'd be made up of the other

00:03:59.750 --> 00:04:00.750
characters that I mentioned.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:05.799
So yes, Shang-Chi and Black Panther were originally
going to be part of the team along with Hawkeye

00:04:05.799 --> 00:04:06.930
and Captain America.

00:04:06.930 --> 00:04:11.349
There's also of course Doctor Strange and
Ant-man who did end up coming into the MCU

00:04:11.349 --> 00:04:15.950
after Civil War and it shows how much things
changed once Marvel started regaining their

00:04:15.950 --> 00:04:16.990
IPs.

00:04:16.990 --> 00:04:21.380
Out of the entire line-up they had only Captain
America and The Avengers ended up actually

00:04:21.380 --> 00:04:25.650
being released in the original 8 years showing
how much stuff can shift about.

00:04:25.650 --> 00:04:30.160
Now along with getting the Iron Man rights
back, they also secured them from other studios.

00:04:30.160 --> 00:04:33.100
Hulk was freed up slightly from Universal
along with Thor from Paramount and Black Widow

00:04:33.100 --> 00:04:34.850
from Lions Gate.

00:04:34.850 --> 00:04:42.210
So you can see how getting all this back started
to change things and interestingly, Tony Stark

00:04:42.210 --> 00:04:44.640
was never supposed to be the face of the MCU.

00:04:44.640 --> 00:04:49.110
It's weird to think about this especially
due to how iconic Robert Downey Juniors portrayal

00:04:49.110 --> 00:04:53.010
is but he was thought of as a character that
they could use to introduce others rather

00:04:53.010 --> 00:04:54.090
than being the main guy.

00:04:54.090 --> 00:04:58.320
The position of power was originally going
to fall to The Hulk who Marvel had had success

00:04:58.320 --> 00:05:02.970
with due to the Ang-Lee movie and of course
the legendary 70s TV show.

00:05:02.970 --> 00:05:07.090
Robert Downey Junior wasn't even really wanted
to be part of the universe at the time due

00:05:07.090 --> 00:05:11.340
to controversy surrounding him and it was
only due to Jon Favreau that they were convinced

00:05:11.340 --> 00:05:12.670
to take the shot.

00:05:12.670 --> 00:05:17.201
His movie was a big success and after Iron
Man was released Marvel announced that the

00:05:17.201 --> 00:05:21.050
other films they had coming out would lead
into the Avengers.

00:05:21.050 --> 00:05:25.170
Slowly things started to all slot into place
with the shared universe plan all coming together

00:05:25.170 --> 00:05:26.430
bit by bit.

00:05:26.430 --> 00:05:30.690
Tony appeared in The Incredible Hulk, Thor
was hinted at in Iron Man 2 and then Thor

00:05:30.690 --> 00:05:34.990
itself ended with a tease to the Avengers
with Captain America showing the first trailer

00:05:34.990 --> 00:05:35.990
for it.

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:39.111
Now from this point onwards, Marvel came to
realise how important that it was to have

00:05:39.111 --> 00:05:43.300
a plan in place and they of course finished
out The Avengers with a tease towards Thanos

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.980
in the post credits scene.

00:05:44.980 --> 00:05:48.950
The studio also started to showcase their
plans far in advance so that they could make

00:05:48.950 --> 00:05:50.561
minor changes to it if needs be.

00:05:50.561 --> 00:05:51.561
Dropping an entire line-up allowed them to
see audience reaction, get ideas for how to

00:05:51.561 --> 00:05:52.561
better tie things together and generally just
shift stuff around.

00:05:52.561 --> 00:05:53.561
If you look at their original plans you'll
see that we were originally supposed to be

00:05:53.561 --> 00:05:54.561
getting Captain America The Serpant society
along with Avengers Infinity War Part 1 and

00:05:54.561 --> 00:05:55.561
2.

00:05:55.561 --> 00:05:56.561
This was of course changed to Endgame and
Serpent society was dropped in favour of Civil

00:05:56.561 --> 00:05:57.561
War.

00:05:57.561 --> 00:05:58.561
Marvel admitted that after Batman V Superman
was announced that they decided to change

00:05:58.561 --> 00:05:59.790
direction and having such a plan laid out
like this allowed them to be reactive and

00:05:59.790 --> 00:06:01.190
see where trends were going.

00:06:01.190 --> 00:06:05.500
There was also Spider-man Homecoming that
originally wasn't part of the lineup but this

00:06:05.500 --> 00:06:08.120
all changed after the Sony Email Hack.

00:06:08.120 --> 00:06:11.760
That studio were heading down the Amazing
Spider-man route but they ended up talking

00:06:11.760 --> 00:06:15.950
it out with Feige and the two sides came to
a deal that allowed him to come back into

00:06:15.950 --> 00:06:16.950
the universe.

00:06:16.950 --> 00:06:21.420
There's also the Inhumans that were dropped
after the series didn't go down too well but

00:06:21.420 --> 00:06:24.380
on the whole Marvel has been a big success.

00:06:24.380 --> 00:06:27.610
They've reached a point now where they've
got back the rights to all their original

00:06:27.610 --> 00:06:32.540
characters and going forward into Phase 5
and 6 we'll be seeing more from the Fantastic

00:06:32.540 --> 00:06:34.680
Four and likely the X-men.

00:06:34.680 --> 00:06:38.450
Some of the stand out things about the original
plan too are characters that we never really

00:06:38.450 --> 00:06:39.850
got in the MCU.

00:06:39.850 --> 00:06:44.760
Though Cloak and Dagger got a show, we still
haven't heard anything about Power Pack and

00:06:44.760 --> 00:06:47.730
they're probably the most obscure characters
on there.

00:06:47.730 --> 00:06:52.710
There's also the Nick Fury movie which I think
we will sort of get when Secret Invasion rolls

00:06:52.710 --> 00:06:53.710
around.

00:06:53.710 --> 00:06:57.440
Looking back at what was originally meant
to be it's kinda crazy to think how things

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:01.910
have changed and it shows the big comeback
journey that Marvel went on.

00:07:01.910 --> 00:07:06.400
Here's an organisation that had to sell filing
cabinets to stay afloat and they now completley

00:07:06.400 --> 00:07:07.550
dominate the industry.

00:07:07.550 --> 00:07:11.850
Though we don't know exactly what the plots
of these movies would have been it's interesting

00:07:11.850 --> 00:07:16.270
to see how it all changed and it really makes
